{"name":"Fresco","hex":"#f4dbd9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fresco","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cool, refreshing state of the air; coolness, duskiness, shade.","An artwork made by applying water-based pigment to wet or fresh lime mortar or plaster."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To paint using fresco."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fresco"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fresco","blocks":[{"text":"Fresco is a technique of mural painting executed upon freshly laid (\"wet\") lime plaster. Water is used as the vehicle for the dry-powder pigment to merge with the plaster, and with the setting of the plaster, the painting becomes an integral part of the wall. The word fresco is derived from the Italian adjective fresco meaning \"fresh\", and may thus be contrasted with fresco-secco or secco mural painting techniques, which are applied to dried plaster, to supplement painting in fresco. The fresco technique has been employed since antiquity and is closely associated with Italian Renaissance painting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Creaci%C3%B3n_de_Ad%C3%A1n_%28Miguel_%C3%81ngel%29.jpg/330px-Creaci%C3%B3n_de_Ad%C3%A1n_%28Miguel_%C3%81ngel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fresco","wikidata":"Q134194"},{"title":"Fresco (M People album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fresco is the fourth studio album by the British dance band M People. It includes the Top 10 singles \"Just for You\" and \"Angel St\", the single \"Fantasy Island\", and a cover version of the Roxy Music song \"Avalon\". The album reached number 2 in the UK Albums Chart, and was supported by a large UK arena tour. The tour confirmed M People as one of the UK's most successful live acts of the 1990s. Fresco became M People's last studio album to date as the group has not released any new material since. Various hit collections followed as well as two solo albums from lead singer Heather Small. By the end of 1998, Fresco had sold over 750,000 copies in the UK."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/46/CD_M_People_Fresco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fresco_(M_People_album)","wikidata":"Q5502901"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Etruskischer_Meister_002.jpg/500px-Etruskischer_Meister_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Etruskischer_Meister_002.jpg/1280px-Etruskischer_Meister_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Etruskischer_Meister_002.jpg/500px-Etruskischer_Meister_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Etruscan fresco. Detail of two dancers from the Tomb of the Triclinium in the Necropolis of Monterozzi 470 BC, Tarquinia, Lazio, Italy.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEtruskischer_Meister_002.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Giovane-seduto.JPG/500px-Giovane-seduto.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Giovane-seduto.JPG/1280px-Giovane-seduto.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Giovane-seduto.JPG/500px-Giovane-seduto.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Roman fresco of a young man from the Villa di Arianna, Stabiae, 1st century AD","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGiovane-seduto.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Giotto_di_Bondone_-_No._18_Scenes_from_the_